    observation:
      "From the air, identify Peneda-Gerês by its exposed granite and boulder-strewn, rounded terrain, distinct from the slate- and gneiss-dominated ranges elsewhere in northern Portugal; man-made reservoirs and small terraced fields are common among the hills.",
    distinguish:
      "Peneda-Gerês and Montesinho to the north-east are both old crystalline ranges, but Peneda-Gerês is dominated by granite with more visible boulders, while Montesinho is mostly slate and gneiss with gentler relief.",
    concept:
      "Established in 1971, Peneda-Gerês National Park is Portugal's only national park, home to wild Garrano mountain ponies and numerous Neolithic stone circles and dolmens.",
    history:
      "Historically isolated by its terrain, the area preserves many traditional granite-built villages and transhumance herding customs, with small-scale seasonal grazing still practised today.",
